1.1 **"Software"** means the software known as Sombra Guardian, including all Source Code, scripts, configuration templates, database migrations, plugins, workflow definitions, tests, and Documentation delivered by Licensor, together with all updates that Licensor elects to provide, but excluding Third-Party Components.

1.2 **"Source Code"** means the human-readable form of the Software.

1.3 **"Documentation"** means the README files, manuals, guides, and other written materials that accompany the Software.

1.4 **"Derivative Works"** means any modification, adaptation, translation, or other work that is based on or incorporates any portion of the Software.

1.5 **"Third-Party Components"** means any software library, dataset, framework, or other material in or used with the Software that is owned by a third party and licensed under that party's own terms, including open-source components.

1.6 **"Authorized Deployment"** means one production installation of the Software, running one Telegram bot identity, operated by or for Licensee. The number of Authorized Deployments granted to Licensee is stated in the Order Form and is one (1) if not stated.

1.7 **"Order Form"** means the document in the form of Schedule A, or any other written or electronic order that identifies Licensee, the Fees, and the license scope, and that Licensor has accepted.

1.8 **"Fees"** means the amounts payable by Licensee under the Order Form.

